infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Saturation beats utilization as a latency signal
  desc The lower-utilization disk is the slow one — what matters is the queue
  compares
    - label Disk A
      children
        - label Utilization 80%
          desc The calmer-looking disk
        - label Queue depth: 50 waiting
          desc Work arrives faster than it drains
        - label Saturated: the real culprit
          desc Every queued job pays the delay
    - label Disk B
      children
        - label Utilization 95%
          desc The busier-looking disk
        - label Queue depth: 1 waiting
          desc Keeping pace with arrivals
        - label Healthy: not the cause
          desc 100% busy is fine if nothing waits
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
